<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:57:20Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>EU court rules against Belgian far-right party in IKEA case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9477e3f054d80ddf5197ca8117dfed6e14df4d4f7897a9a4e8288497ab7a5a1</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-court-rules-against-belgian-far-right-party-in-ikea-case/a-79159207--531c0db38ccd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-court-rules-against-belgian-far-right-party-in-ikea-case/a-79159207?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A European court has backed Ikea's challenge against a Belgian far-right party, saying the use of Ikea-style visuals could harm the company's reputation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK announces trade sanctions on Israeli settlements in occupied West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3602a38852bb8ffd950e69c683c0a7b1fbf88a9a789379e1d529c5549b34b55</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-announces-trade-sanctions-on-israeli-settlements-in-occupied-west-bank/a-79155051--d2a4da122a4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-announces-trade-sanctions-on-israeli-settlements-in-occupied-west-bank/a-79155051?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Foreign Secretary Ed Miliband said the measures were in response to what he called "settler terrorism" in the occupied territories. The measures are part of the UK's efforts to support a two-state solution.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Japan's empty temples seek new ways to survive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca0cfcf36c5bc4f84d8e3bb792cf9e75d37763af79b620cb3bf8179c92605f82</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:41Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964--7eea677a26bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With a declining population, shrinking congregations and growing economic pressures, temples are struggling to stay relevant. As more temples are sold or closed, is religion in decline in modern Japan?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Afghanistan's women: A national soccer team without a home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc2f00c3b2c32e0331e1ccd086e1be4a9f834ca7e998425558a097755c78a123</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:44Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500--7cfb666b9c3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Afghan women's national football team has finally been officially recognized by FIFA. Now the players want to make history both on and off the field.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>German police arrest suspect in power grid sabotage case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a15b05b247fb8906720850b020946807e5ec08f1c899c476aaf230f7a756502</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-arrest-suspect-in-power-grid-sabotage-case/a-79161142--0b56d3da8acf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-arrest-suspect-in-power-grid-sabotage-case/a-79161142?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators say the suspect used homemade rockets and conductive wire to target high-voltage lines in three German states, apparently as part of a campaign against fossil fuels.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary orders 10 Russian diplomats to leave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2abf0df5ed4bb84559aac3e060282f781adde037d182beecec67da346bd734ca</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-orders-10-russian-diplomats-to-leave/a-79157576--560dc3bd8df1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-orders-10-russian-diplomats-to-leave/a-79157576?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Budapest says the expulsions are necessary to protect security and sovereignty after years of comparatively close ties between Hungary and Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US-Canada tariff dispute weighs on cross-border ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53dc2dae2464aa823232983c17807900bb74ab8c4e872fe1f0b66a3aa479cb92</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:53Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-canada-tariff-dispute-weighs-on-cross-border-ties/a-78815803--082b25646c1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-canada-tariff-dispute-weighs-on-cross-border-ties/a-78815803?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Canada's retaliatory tariffs take effect, Canadian and US car industries fear the trade war will hit them hard, while Canadians are cutting back on travel.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Crackdown on foreign traders prompts xenophobia fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a88bafdd5aebe7c65fe24802696de5dcd18852659fc9ab8d179590234949b5af</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:56Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-crackdown-on-foreign-traders-prompts-xenophobia-fears/a-79143847--a8e571d0a365.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-crackdown-on-foreign-traders-prompts-xenophobia-fears/a-79143847?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fears of xenophobia are rising in Kenya after President William Ruto ordered a crackdown on foreigners working as hawkers. The government insists however that legally documented foreign traders remain protected.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Australia targets big tech with algorithm opt-out bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22427ba0a88e939d4749be28ce281250c7fc1ba8314d0e08f11009375a7d62a5</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:56:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-targets-big-tech-with-algorithm-opt-out-bill/a-79154108--95b8ccd62504.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-targets-big-tech-with-algorithm-opt-out-bill/a-79154108?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The "My Feed, My Way," legislation would require the likes of Facebook, TikTok and Instagram to let users opt out of algorithms or risk heavy fines.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Renoir Museum robbery: 2 paintings missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f69673c64f9cd097e4f92101ba305e13b9c1c970732bc8d18389f1d1e82b0b3</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:57:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T07:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/renoir-museum-robbery-2-paintings-missing/a-79154458--4fcf4fff5ab0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/renoir-museum-robbery-2-paintings-missing/a-79154458?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police are on the hunt for thieves who stole two paintings from the Renoir Museum on the French Riviera in an overnight heist. Two other stolen works were abandoned as they fled.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>PISA test reveals alarming drop in reading and math skills</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06469bd2e9ada99f65d8e526eb62235515409d7b3b01cd2bf132a53fae3337d6</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:57:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T07:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pisa-test-reveals-alarming-drop-in-reading-and-math-skills/a-79147293--6fcb0a53f051.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pisa-test-reveals-alarming-drop-in-reading-and-math-skills/a-79147293?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2025 results from the influential global study show a downward trend in students' performance. Germany's 15-year-olds are faring worse than ever.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c4b47a05084c4b8e2c0c44b0fd9b009ac48bcba75e34fe488404efaf9b4a615</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Female footballers offered egg freezing but doubts remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8760aa1710067e64f73a8221428abc8c638206425ebae93027857bfcef966da</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:57:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/female-footballers-offered-egg-freezing-but-doubts-remain/a-79145259--e96625275f81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/female-footballers-offered-egg-freezing-but-doubts-remain/a-79145259?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's football federation are set to join a handful of clubs in paying for female players to freeze their eggs during their careers. While players have pushed for the move, there are welfare concerns too.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Hindu group apologizes over Eiffel Tower row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e50ee82b8bb7b38506ede89b2dbd21a5943df9b961cbb134f7fcfb5cb21807bb</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:57:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-hindu-group-apologizes-over-eiffel-tower-row/live-79153937--9288b3e28d91.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-hindu-group-apologizes-over-eiffel-tower-row/live-79153937?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After the Eiffel Tower was closed amid a staff strike over alleged discrimination, Hindu group BAPS issued an apology, but maintained that no one was denied access. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Gas reserves historically low ahead of winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:baa53d014544989d85a2306f8568d17e7dca230a84ff33f3006e9036a590aad7</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:57:14Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-gas-reserves-historically-low-ahead-of-winter/live-79153944--dc1a84dcb659.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-gas-reserves-historically-low-ahead-of-winter/live-79153944?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Gas storage operator association INES has warned that Germany's gas reserves could run out in the event of a cold winter. Meanwhile, fallout from the AfD's state election victory continues. Follow DW for the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump threatens to block Canada's Bombardier planes from US market</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15a4f8433fa2d7d2eca093abd2ae15503bc3ec935373931ec38f6cb9c27371c0</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:57:17Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T05:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-threatens-to-block-canada-s-bombardier-planes-from-us-market/a-79153896--6b1efc0bb44d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-threatens-to-block-canada-s-bombardier-planes-from-us-market/a-79153896?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trump says Bombardier must build aircraft in the US as Canada imposes tariffs of up to 50% on US imports.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine updates: Two killed in Kyiv as 3-day truce ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd1724fb17ba0d3429a5b5c52356102caf3935ef0fbb20f52655ca3a08d544f5</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:57:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T03:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-explosions-rock-kyiv-as-3-day-truce-ends/live-79153168--19acbc68fd39.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-updates-two-killed-in-kyiv-as-3-day-truce-ends/live-79153168?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A series of explosions rocked Kyiv and neighboring cities signaling the end of Russia's three-day ceasefire. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Eiffel Tower employees strike after female staff removed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9364cd8496cc7a735b8d46c187085dc3896f1f9476e89ad2f5a6f98e1a7c0a7</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T22:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eiffel-tower-employees-strike-after-female-staff-removed/a-79152603--a226c210998d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eiffel-tower-employees-strike-after-female-staff-removed/a-79152603?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The employees protested against the removal of the site's female workers due to a request by a visiting Hindu group. The tower's operating company apologized for the decision.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>3 years on, Morocco earthquake victims still wait for help</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:278b59db5a76ce071b38eeebf58914b6a2817278c350ca8f746d1948f9ec4123</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/3-years-on-morocco-earthquake-victims-still-wait-for-help/a-78874844--12aebab2298e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/3-years-on-morocco-earthquake-victims-still-wait-for-help/a-78874844?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Reconstruction has progressed in the three years since the 2023 Morocco earthquake, but some survivors are still living in tents. Locals are divided as to how successful it's been, and whether state aid is enough.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c388abbb4171042f1d1173ef20d74055a4e7c27b0af7a97b754efdb7ff16b33</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Nicaragua challenges German arms exports to Israel at ICJ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f0809fba5927a8ec7201fb8385eccacd75bccf193f69bbb33110d8d048cb1a9c</id><updated>2026-09-08T12:55:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044--315737afbbdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has asked the International Court of Justice to dismiss the case on jurisdiction grounds. It also said its arms exports to Israel were documented, published, and subject to more stringent checks than most.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
